---
layout: layout.njk
---
<section class="hero">
  <p class="kicker mono">CIS 9000 · IT STRATEGY · PRACTICE CONSOLE</p>
  <h1>Good evening. Ready to practice?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Short weekly question sets that mirror the exam’s case-based reasoning. Miss a question and PAL brings it back on a spaced schedule — that’s the part that makes it stick. You hand in your completion log just twice all semester — from <a href="/systems/">SYSTEMS</a>, once before each test.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="missions-h">
  <h2 id="missions-h" class="panel-label mono">MISSION SELECT</h2>
  {% for s in sets %}
  <section class="set-block" aria-labelledby="set-{{ s.set }}-h">
    <h3 id="set-{{ s.set }}-h" class="set-head mono"><span>{{ s.heading }}</span><span class="set-status" data-set-status="{{ s.set }}"></span></h3>
    <ol class="mission-list">
      {% for n in s.weeks %}
      {% set w = bank.weeks | findWeek(n) %}
      <li>
        {% if w %}
        <a class="mission" href="/week-{{ w.week }}/" data-week="{{ w.week }}">
          <span class="mission-num mono">W{{ w.week | pad2 }}</span>
          <span class="mission-title">{{ w.title }}</span>
          <span class="mission-meta mono"><span class="mission-count">{{ w.questions.length }} Q</span><span class="mission-status" data-week-status="{{ w.week }}"></span></span>
        </a>
        {% else %}
        <span class="mission mission-locked">
          <span class="mission-num mono">W{{ n | pad2 }}</span>
          <span class="mission-title">Releases after that week’s class</span>
          <span class="mission-meta mono">LOCKED</span>
        </span>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="review-h" class="review-panel">
  <h2 id="review-h" class="panel-label mono">REVIEW QUEUE</h2>
  <a class="mission mission-review" href="/review/">
    <span class="mission-num mono" aria-hidden="true">RQ</span>
    <span class="mission-title">Review missed questions</span>
    <span class="mission-meta mono" id="review-count">—</span>
  </a>
  <p class="hint">Every question you practice comes back on a spaced schedule — about 1, 3, then 7 days. A quick correct answer at each step locks it in for good.</p>
</section>

<section class="install-hint" id="install-hint" aria-labelledby="install-h" hidden>
  <h2 id="install-h" class="panel-label mono">KEEP PAL IN YOUR POCKET</h2>
  <p>Installing PAL puts it on your home screen, makes it work better with no signal, and keeps the browser from clearing the progress you’ve saved.</p>
  <p class="install-steps"><span class="mono">IPHONE</span> tap ••• or the Share button → Add to Home Screen<br>
    <span class="mono">ANDROID</span> browser menu → Add to Home screen</p>
  <p class="install-warn">One catch on iPhone: the installed app gets its own separate copy of your saved data, so the progress you’ve made in the browser won’t appear there. Download or copy a backup in <a href="/systems/">SYSTEMS</a> first, then restore it in the app.</p>
  <div class="act">
    <button class="btn-ghost" type="button" id="install-hint-dismiss">GOT IT</button>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="module" src="/assets/js/home.js"></script>
